│ patch_description        │ The current algorithm routes every partition of every destination along the single        │
│                          │ cheapest Dijkstra path. This creates heavy congestion on shared links and ignores         │
│                          │ alternative low-cost routes. Improvement: for each (dst, partition) pair, pick from the   │
│                          │ k-shortest simple paths (by cost), cycling across them so partitions are spread over      │
│                          │ disjoint/diverse routes. This reduces redundant transfers on the same links, balances     │
│                          │ load across networks, and exploits multi-network topologies to lower total cost. Since    │
│                          │ cost likely depends on congestion/flow on edges, spreading partitions across parallel     │
│                          │ paths lowers per-edge flow and total cost.                                                │
