│ patch_name               │ ksp_diverse_partition_paths                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ The current algorithm sends every partition of a destination along the exact same single  │
│                          │ shortest path, causing all partitions to redundantly traverse the same (potentially       │
│                          │ expensive) links and concentrate load on one route. A better strategy: (1) compute        │
│                          │ k-shortest simple paths per destination using Yen's algorithm, (2) select a diverse set   │
│                          │ of paths — cycling through the k candidates so partitions are spread across parallel      │
│                          │ routes/networks, reducing per-link congestion and leveraging multi-network topologies,    │
│                          │ and (3) reweigh edges dynamically by adding a congestion penalty proportional to how many │
│                          │ partitions already used that edge, which balances load across networks. If k-shortest     │
│                          │ paths fail for some destination, fall back to Dijkstra. This reduces redundant transfers, │
│                          │ spreads cost across cheaper parallel links, and exploits multiple egress routes to        │
│                          │ minimize total transfer cost.                                                             │
