╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ steiner_multicast_optimizer                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ Restructured the broadcast routing around a two-stage multicast planning architecture     │
│                          │ instead of independent per-destination shortest paths:                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **GraphSanitizer / DistanceIndex**: A preprocessing layer that cleans the graph        │
│                          │ (removes self-loops, inbound source edges, and unusable zero-cost links) and computes a   │
│                          │ single Dijkstra pass from the source, indexing distances and predecessor chains once —    │
│                          │ reused by all lookups instead of recomputing per destination.                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **SteinerTreeBuilder**: A multicast tree planner using the shortest-path heuristic     │
│                          │ (metric-closure MST mapped back onto real paths). Destinations sharing backbone links now │
│                          │ reuse them, eliminating redundant transfers of every partition over repeated edges. Edges │
│                          │ are deduplicated across overlapping paths, so each shared link carries traffic once       │
│                          │ instead of once-per-destination.                                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **MulticastTopologyAssembler**: A builder that walks each destination's unique route   │
│                          │ inside the shared tree and populates the `BroadCastTopology` per partition, preserving    │
│                          │ the original output format exactly.                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This lowers total data transfer cost by consolidating overlapping per-destination routes  │
│                          │ into shared backbone paths (Steiner-tree behavior), improves maintainability through      │
│                          │ clean separation (sanitization → indexing → tree construction → assembly), and keeps the  │
│                          │ same inputs/outputs as the original `search_algorithm`, `BroadCastTopology`, and          │
│                          │ `make_nx_graph`.                                                                          │
