│ patch_name               │ k_shortest_paths_per_partition                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ The current algorithm sends every partition of every destination along the single         │
│                          │ cheapest Dijkstra path. This overloads the cheapest link (its price/cost typically rises  │
│                          │ with congestion, or throughput caps throttle completion), and it ignores alternative      │
│                          │ routes. A better strategy: compute the k-shortest simple paths from src to each dst (by   │
│                          │ cost), then assign partitions round-robin across these candidate paths, effectively       │
│                          │ spreading the load over parallel low-cost routes and exploiting multi-network topologies. │
│                          │ This reduces redundant transfers on any single link and balances load across networks,    │
│                          │ lowering overall cost.                                                                    │
