╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ multipath_load_balanced_search                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ The current algorithm naively uses single-source Dijkstra for every destination, which    │
│                          │ (a) forces all partitions of a destination down the same path, overloading low-cost links │
│                          │ (throughput is a hard constraint, so congestion inflates effective cost) and (b)          │
│                          │ recomputes paths redundantly for each destination.                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The proposed edit: (1) compute k-shortest paths per destination using Yen's algorithm,    │
│                          │ (2) iteratively pick paths that minimize cost *after* accounting for congestion — edges   │
│                          │ already carrying flow from previously routed partitions get their effective cost scaled   │
│                          │ up, spreading load across parallel networks/links, and (3) alternate partitions among the │
│                          │ top-k candidate paths so partitions of the same destination traverse different            │
│                          │ (overlapping/non-overlapping) low-cost routes, exploiting multi-network topologies        │
│                          │ instead of funneling everything through one cheapest path. This reduces cost by avoiding  │
│                          │ congestion-induced slow transfers and by distributing flow over cheaper parallel edges,   │
│                          │ while remaining a pure drop-in replacement for `search_algorithm`.                        │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
