│ patch_description        │ The current algorithm sends every partition of the data along the exact same shortest     │
│                          │ path (computed once per dst), so all partitions redundantly traverse the same links,      │
│                          │ driving up cost and congestion. A better strategy: for each destination, compute multiple │
│                          │ edge-disjoint low-cost paths (using short path enumeration with a cost cap) and assign    │
│                          │ different partitions to different paths. This spreads load across networks/links, avoids  │
│                          │ redundant transfers over the same expensive edges, and exploits multi-network topologies. │
│                          │ Additionally, paths should be sorted by cost so the cheapest paths carry partitions       │
│                          │ first.                                                                                    │
