                        Patch Metadata - Gen 11/200 - Novelty: 1/3 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/3                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ congestion_aware_ksp_broadcast                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ The current algorithm sends every partition of every destination along the single         │
│                          │ shortest path. This (a) overloads one network path when many partitions/dsts share it and │
│                          │ (b) never exploits alternative parallel paths. I propose two targeted improvements:       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Congestion-aware weights**: maintain a running count of how many partition-flows     │
│                          │ have already been placed on each edge. Before routing each destination, create an         │
│                          │ auxiliary weighted copy of the graph where each edge's effective cost is `cost * (1 +     │
│                          │ usage)` (scaled). This spreads load across parallel network links, which reduces          │
│                          │ bottleneck cost in multi-cloud topologies where transferring many partitions              │
│                          │ simultaneously over one link is more expensive than splitting across several links.       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **k-shortest-path partition assignment**: instead of putting all partitions of a dst   │
│                          │ on one path, enumerate up to `num_partitions` simple paths via `nx.shortest_simple_paths` │
│                          │ (with congestion-adjusted weights) and assign partitions round-robin across them. This    │
│                          │ leverages multi-network parallelism and reduces redundant per-link load.                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Cost per edge is still summed correctly by downstream evaluation since the topology       │
│                          │ format is unchanged — we only change which paths are chosen.                              │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
