│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ disjoint_partition_routing_with_overlay_multicast                                         │
│ patch_description        │ The current algorithm routes every partition along the same single shortest path per      │
│                          │ destination, causing redundant transfers over shared edges and ignoring multi-network     │
│                          │ parallel paths. A much cheaper broadcast structure is a two-level overlay: (1) build a    │
│                          │ minimum-cost Steiner-like multicast tree from src to all destinations at the *aggregate*  │
│                          │ level using shortest-path distances (this shares links, so the data is sent over each     │
│                          │ tree edge only once instead of num_partitions times), and (2) assign each partition a     │
│                          │ different parallel path (k shortest node/edge-disjoint paths) so load is balanced across  │
│                          │ networks and no single bottleneck link carries all partitions. This reduces total cost    │
│                          │ both by multicast sharing (avoiding redundant src->relay transfers) and by spreading      │
│                          │ partitions across disjoint low-cost routes.                                               │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
