│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ k_shortest_paths_shared_prefix                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ The current algorithm computes a single Dijkstra shortest path per destination and then   │
│                          │ naively duplicates every edge for every partition. This inflates cost because (a) it      │
│                          │ recomputes Dijkstra from scratch per destination, and (b) it ignores cheaper alternative  │
│                          │ paths and shared transfer segments that can amortize cost across partitions.              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The proposed edit improves `search_algorithm` by:                                         │
│                          │ 1. Computing single-source shortest paths once (from `src`) instead of running Dijkstra   │
│                          │ once per destination — an efficiency win and identical-quality baseline routing.          │
│                          │ 2. Considering the top-k shortest simple paths per destination (via                       │
│                          │ `nx.shortest_simple_paths`) and picking the cheapest path by summed edge cost, which      │
│                          │ allows exploiting alternative multi-network routes that plain Dijkstra on raw cost may    │
│                          │ miss when capacity/throughput penalties apply.                                            │
│                          │ 3. Deduplicating edge-level entries so shared edges within a partition's path are         │
│                          │ recorded once, reducing redundant transfer records.                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This reduces total data transfer cost while keeping all configurations runnable           │
│                          │ (success_rate preserved) and better balancing load across available networks.             │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
