│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ multipath_dijkstra_broadcast                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ This crossover combines the efficiency of the single-source Dijkstra pre-computation from │
│                          │ the prior program with a per-partition multipath strategy. Key improvements:              │
│                          │ 1. Compute single-source Dijkstra once instead of per-destination, reducing routing       │
│                          │ overhead.                                                                                 │
│                          │ 2. For each partition, draw from the generator of k-shortest simple paths so different    │
│                          │ partitions can traverse different (parallel) routes, spreading load across networks and   │
│                          │ avoiding bottleneck links.                                                                │
│                          │ 3. Dedupe shared edges within a partition's path to avoid redundant transfer records.     │
│                          │ 4. Fall back safely to Dijkstra paths when a destination is unreachable or k-shortest     │
│                          │ iteration fails, preserving the original program's robustness and identical output        │
│                          │ format.                                                                                   │
