│ patch_name               │ steiner_edge_sharing_paths                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the naive per-destination Dijkstra in search_algorithm with a Steiner-tree-like   │
│                          │ edge-sharing approach. First compute shortest paths from src to all destinations once via │
│                          │ nx.single_source_dijkstra, then iteratively build a shared directed tree: start from src, │
│                          │ and repeatedly attach the "closest" reachable destination (in terms of path cost over the │
│                          │ sanitized graph), adding its path edges to the tree. Once an edge is in the tree, later   │
│                          │ destinations reuse those edges — the edge cost is only counted once in the tree, but per  │
│                          │ the recommendation we still append each destination's src→dst path (composed of tree      │
│                          │ edges) to the BroadCastTopology, so edge data is shared across destinations and redundant │
│                          │ transfers are reduced by the evaluator's edge-sharing accounting. All edge lookups read   │
│                          │ from the sanitized directed graph h (never G), preserving the validated I/O contract of   │
│                          │ append_dst_partition_path with whole-edge appends. Using single_source_dijkstra once is   │
│                          │ also faster than repeated Dijkstra calls, improving runtime.                              │
