│ patch_description        │ Replace independent per-destination shortest paths with a Steiner-tree-like shared        │
│                          │ backbone. We iteratively grow a shared directed tree from src using Dijkstra on the       │
│                          │ sanitized graph h, merging each destination's shortest path into the tree only once       │
│                          │ (edges already in the tree are reused for free). Then each destination's path is read     │
│                          │ from the tree. This shares edges across destinations, reducing total transfer cost while  │
│                          │ keeping the exact same output contract (per-dst, per-partition edge appends with [s, t,   │
│                          │ G]). All edge data is read from G only for the final append, pathfinding on h only,       │
│                          │ matching the validated Gen 0 behavior.                                                    │
