│ patch_description        │ Restructure into a modular pipeline: (1) a graph prep stage, (2) a single multicast       │
│                          │ Steiner-tree builder using the closest-attachment heuristic (Dijkstra from each remaining │
│                          │ destination to the current tree via the reversed graph), and (3) a topology writer. The   │
│                          │ key structural change versus the current program: the tree is built **once** and reused   │
│                          │ for all partitions, and per-destination paths are reconstructed by walking up the parent  │
│                          │ map, with an unreachable-node guard (`nx.has_path` / try/except) so no destination causes │
│                          │ a crash. Dedup of tree edges and reuse across all partitions minimizes redundant          │
│                          │ transfers while keeping load balanced and the output format identical.                    │
