│                          │ cost (1035.14), while the perturbed/parallel variant cost more (1412.44) due to           │
│                          │ round-robin load spreading pushing partitions onto costlier routes. The new code keeps    │
│                          │ the cost-minimizing core (all partitions use the globally cheapest path) but strengthens  │
│                          │ the search: it generates candidates via (a) Dijkstra on true cost, (b) perturbed-cost     │
│                          │ Dijkstra variants, and (c) k-shortest simple paths, then picks the single path with       │
│                          │ minimal true edge cost per destination. Missing costs are backfilled with a large finite  │
│                          │ penalty so the search never crashes, but unknown-cost links are effectively avoided when  │
│                          │ any real-cost route exists. This preserves the low-cost behavior of the current best      │
│                          │ program while broadening exploration to reliably find cheaper parallel routes when they   │
│                          │ exist.                                                                                    │
