│ patch_description        │ The Steiner-tree multicast approach achieved the best cost (759.09) by deduplicating      │
│                          │ shared transfers, while the PathOracle/TreeCostModel approach contributed the idea of     │
│                          │ marginal-cost greedy assignment with a shared-edge accounting model. The crossover builds │
│                          │ the Steiner tree once (as in the best program), then refines it with the shared-edge      │
│                          │ greedy: for each destination we consider the tree path plus up to k alternative shortest  │
│                          │ simple paths, and select the one with the lowest marginal cost given edges already        │
│                          │ committed (used edges are free). Destinations are processed in order of tree-path cost so │
│                          │ the cheapest, most-shareable routes commit first. Each partition reuses the final         │
│                          │ per-destination routes, keeping shared edges transferred only once while allowing a       │
│                          │ destination to take a cheap alternate path when it beats its tree path. This preserves    │
│                          │ the exact BroadCastTopology API and output format.                                        │
