│ patch_name               │ backfill_none_cost_penalty                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Backfill `cost=None` edges with a large finite penalty (1e6) in the sanitized internal    │
│                          │ graph used by routing. This makes shortest-path computation deterministic and safe:       │
│                          │ previously, Dijkstra's behavior on None weights was undefined (it happened to work in     │
│                          │ some configs, crashed in others). With an explicit penalty, the router will strongly      │
│                          │ prefer edges with known real costs, and future heuristics can safely compare candidate    │
│                          │ path costs without None crashes. The sanitized graph `h` is internal only — the returned  │
│                          │ edge data still comes from the original graph `G`, so outputs are unchanged where costs   │
│                          │ already exist. I also fix the `_path_cost`/`edge_cost_fn` to use a safe accessor          │
│                          │ consistent with this.                                                                     │
