├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ tm_steiner_tree_broadcast                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the naive per-destination Dijkstra broadcast with a Takahashi-Matsuyama-style     │
│                          │ Steiner tree heuristic. We grow a shared tree from the source: for each remaining         │
│                          │ destination we run multi-source Dijkstra from all current tree nodes to find the cheapest │
│                          │ attachment point, attach the cheapest destination, and record only the *new* edges (dedup │
│                          │ via seen_edges) for each partition. This eliminates redundant transfers over edges shared │
│                          │ by multiple destinations, since each shared edge is only paid once per partition rather   │
│                          │ than once per destination. All edges of the tree are still appended for each partition    │
│                          │ (required so every partition can reach every destination), but overlapping path segments  │
│                          │ across destinations are deduplicated per partition.                                       │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
