│ patch_description        │ The current tree-building loop rebuilds `h.reverse(copy=True)` and re-runs Dijkstra for   │
│                          │ every remaining destination in every while-iteration, for every partition. The reversed   │
│                          │ graph never changes, so cache it once. Since the tree construction depends on nothing     │
│                          │ partition-dependent, the tree is identical across partitions — build it once and reuse    │
│                          │ the resulting `tree_parent` map for all `j`. Also cache the per-dst Dijkstra results      │
│                          │ since distances from a node in the reversed graph don't change during tree construction   │
│                          │ (paths are recorded, not mutated). This produces identical output paths while cutting     │
│                          │ runtime dramatically.                                                                     │
