│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ steiner_broadcast_tree                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ Key idea: broadcasting each partition independently via per-destination shortest paths    │
│                          │ sends the same source-edge segment repeatedly for every destination. Since all partitions │
│                          │ and destinations share the same source, we can drastically cut cost by building a         │
│                          │ *Steiner-like multicast tree* per partition: send each partition once along a shared      │
│                          │ tree, reusing already-paid edges for subsequent destinations.                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Algorithm per partition (and per destination batch):                                      │
│                          │ 1. Clean the graph (remove src in-edges and self loops).                                  │
│                          │ 2. Guard reachability with `nx.has_path`; unreachable destinations are recorded and never │
│                          │ emit empty/partial paths, fixing the silent-drop bug from prior generations.              │
│                          │ 3. Greedy Steiner construction: start with tree = {src}. Repeatedly run Dijkstra *from    │
│                          │ the current tree nodes* to all not-yet-connected destinations, pick the closest           │
│                          │ destination, and attach its shortest path into the tree. Shared edges already paid for in │
│                          │ this partition are traversed at zero incremental cost, so subsequent branches only pay    │
│                          │ for new edges.                                                                            │
│                          │ 4. Each destination's path within the tree is a complete src→dst chain (verified by       │
│                          │ walking tree parents), so every (dst, partition) has a full edge list or is provably      │
│                          │ unreachable.                                                                              │
│                          │ 5. Across partitions, edges are re-paid (partition data is distinct), but within a        │
│                          │ partition the tree eliminates all redundant segment duplication — the dominant cost in    │
│                          │ the baseline (which paid src→…→hop edges once *per destination per partition*).           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This keeps identical inputs/outputs (same `BroadCastTopology` structure,                  │
│                          │ `append_dst_partition_path` calls with `[s, t, G]` triples) while minimizing total        │
│                          │ transfer cost.                                                                            │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
