│ patch_name               │ sort_dsts_cheapest_first                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Sort destinations by ascending true Dijkstra cost from src before constructing the shared │
│                          │ multicast tree. This ensures the backbone forms along the cheapest central paths first,   │
│                          │ and expensive/far destinations hook onto the already-cheap tree rather than locking in an │
│                          │ expensive first backbone. The tree builder already attaches each subsequent destination   │
│                          │ to the existing tree, so processing order directly affects tree quality. Cost             │
│                          │ sanitization is also added to avoid None-weight crashes.                                  │
