│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ steiner_multicast_tree_with_sweep                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ The current program sends each destination independently along its shortest path, paying  │
│                          │ for shared edges multiple times (once per dst that uses them). The best prior program     │
│                          │ (total_cost 759.09 vs 1035.14) built a greedy Steiner multicast tree where edges shared   │
│                          │ between destinations are paid only once. We adopt that improved approach: grow a tree     │
│                          │ from src using multi-source Dijkstra from the current tree, attach the cheapest remaining │
│                          │ destination, and record each tree edge once per partition per destination. Additionally,  │
│                          │ following the recommendation, we sweep a discount factor: attachment cost for             │
│                          │ already-shared edges is discounted (edge cost * (1 - discount)) so higher discounts push  │
│                          │ more traffic onto shared trunks; we build a tree for each discount in {0.0, 0.05, 0.1,    │
│                          │ 0.3, 0.5} and keep the tree with the lowest true incremental cost. This internal search   │
│                          │ is cheap (small graphs) and avoids any scoring-contract risk.                             │
