│ patch_description        │ The best-scoring prior program (total_cost 759.09 vs 1035.14 for plain Dijkstra) built a  │
│                          │ Steiner-like multicast tree: for each partition it grows a shared tree from src,          │
│                          │ attaching the nearest destination via multi-source Dijkstra over the current tree so      │
│                          │ shared trunk edges are only paid once, then reconstructs each dst's chain from parent     │
│                          │ pointers. I re-adopt that strategy, keeping the per-dst Dijkstra fallback guard for       │
│                          │ safety. This eliminates redundant per-destination transfers and exploits shared low-cost  │
│                          │ routes across the multi-network topology.                                                 │
