│ patch_description        │ The current Steiner-tree program already achieves the lowest cost (759.09). The           │
│                          │ recommendation says to try destination-ordering: sort destinations by ascending true      │
│                          │ Dijkstra cost from src so cheap central paths form the backbone first, then far           │
│                          │ destinations attach onto the shared tree. I keep the incremental greedy Steiner tree      │
│                          │ construction (multi-source Dijkstra from tree nodes), but seed the attachment order by    │
│                          │ ascending single-source Dijkstra distance. I also build the tree once and reuse it across │
│                          │ all partitions (the tree per partition is identical since the graph doesn't change),      │
│                          │ reducing runtime. All sanitization, path-reconstruction guards, and append logic are      │
│                          │ preserved.                                                                                │
